{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992624-airplanes-and-trains-vs-moonbridges-and-trods","id":992624,"title":"Airplanes and Trains vs Moonbridges and Trods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T16:45:42-07:00","id":992624,"title":"Airplanes and Trains vs Moonbridges and Trods","content":"Any thoughts on using conventional transportation vs Supernatural.<br /> <br /> advantages and disadvantages.<br /> <br /> oh for silent striders working on a circuit any advantages/disadvantages to the hospitality of other Garou and kin, versus staying a motel<br /> <br /> he'd probaly feel obliged to give them some kind of gift in return for hospitality if he was taxing a kinfolks household.<br /> <br /> one disadvantage I can see is you may not WANT the sept to know your around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-24-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:39:36-07:00","id":992874,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with conventional travel, esp. forms that take a significant amount of time is simple: people.<br /> <br /> Airports and airplanes are frequently stressful enough without Rage and the Curse messing things up. Or a vampire getting peckish and risking a frenzy. Or a changeling running into high banality people in a confined space. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T05:29:26-07:00","id":992895,"title":"","content":"Plus, STORY! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T06:42:10-07:00","id":992920,"title":"","content":"how will vampires travel then lacking any equilivent of moonbridges, or trods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:33:01-07:00","id":992939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992624-airplanes-and-trains-vs-moonbridges-and-trods?p=992920#post992920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how will vampires travel then lacking any equilivent of moonbridges, or trods?</div> </div> </div> </div>FedEx.UPS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T11:01:27-07:00","id":993017,"title":"","content":"Traditionally speaking, most vampires don't travel much because it's hard for them to do so. Travel for most vampires requires a lot of preparation, and using methods that are either more time consuming (such as taking shorter bus/train rides from town to town so they can stop, figure out a temporary haven, find a snack, and repeat), or expensive (private flights/transports with ghouls running the travel). Most vampires that travel frequently have access to Protean and Animalism to allow for easier survival between cities, or travel with humans that are living a similar lifestyle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T19:32:17-07:00","id":993253,"title":"","content":"Both general forms of travel are options, the characters shouldn't be pressed for one over the other unless under very specific circumstances. Don't go for Special as default, or it can loose its &quot;specialness&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, usually special travel is dangerous and somewhat time-consuming. It is important to note that they were considered fast and reliable in the past, when every travel was long and dangerous. On a daily basis it is easier to just take a buss, train or airplane. And that's just fine. This is a game of <u>modern</u> horror, and it would make no sense for the characters being all the time separated from humanity. It should even highlight their necessity and insistence on being apart.<br /> <br /> Special travel usually does have a lot of distinct advantages, though. First, it is available on circumstances where mundane travel maybe isn't. If the characters are trapped in the Caern in some way, then the Moon Bridge can be their only option. Second, it is far easier to not be detected, and sometimes it is a serious issue. Third, depending on circumstances it can be your only route for your destiny, or actually faster, or strategically favorable. Forth, sometimes the destiny is in the very route used. If the mystery lies in the highway, going there by Trod could not be the best choice. If it lies in the Trod itself, it is another matter entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:12:52-07:00","id":993275,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on the thing about a Silent strider and &quot;Stay with local sept vs, check out a hotel room&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:26:34-07:00","id":993379,"title":"","content":"It's entirely situational?<br /> <br /> A Strider might be on good terms with a Sept and stay there as an accepted guest as a given because of it, a Sept might not like the Strider at all and insist the Strider stay with their people while in their Protectorate as a formality, etc.<br /> <br /> Most Striders are going to have to be highly adaptable unless they travel a fairly tight and well known circuit between a few spots they're well known in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:43:03-07:00","id":993489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/992624-airplanes-and-trains-vs-moonbridges-and-trods?p=993275#post993275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on the thing about a Silent strider and &quot;Stay with local sept vs, check out a hotel room&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They're often the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:54:52-07:00","id":994916,"title":"","content":"Striders usually keep good relations with septs abroad, first as a tribe, second on an individual level, out of necessity. That makes it a higher probability for them to stay at a sept.<br /> <br /> Not having money is also a common reason, though not an universal one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T22:16:34-07:00","id":995511,"title":"","content":"Then you have Mages, whose situation is at once simpler and more complicated.<br /> <br /> With mundane travel, they have the advantage of being entirely mortal, without any sort of weird psychological hangups that make interacting with people difficult (other than Quiet and Resonance/Synergy). They have no time limits, need for blood snacks, or vulnerabilities to banality.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the lives of Mages are complicated, for multiple reasons. Just because they don't have an in-built complication with mass transit, doesn't rule out <i>Paradigm-specific</i> complications. A Shaman needs to observe any taboos or requirements foisted on them by their spirit allies, which can either interfere with traveling on a plane or bus, or else make said travel awkward for everyone involved. &quot;No sir, I don't want any food in exchange for my 'hospitality'. Stay behind the line and stop talking to me. I'm trying to drive the bus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention the Shaman also needs to stop to converse with the local spirits whenever they arrive at a new place, because it would be rude to do otherwise. A Chorister needs to stop at a chapel of some kind to pray when the holy day of the week comes up. It's worse for Islamic Choristers, who need to pray five times a day, which is inconvenient for someone on a bus or plane.<br /> <br /> Then you have a lot of Mages who use weapons as Instruments for their magic. Carrying concealed firearms or longswords is doable on a bus or train, but impossible on a plane. Not unless you start weaving spells to fool airport security measures. It gets especially awkward when your weapon is a treasured artifact and Unique Instrument, that cannot be replaced. If airport security confiscates it, good luck getting it back (assuming you aren't just arrested). Drugs can be a similar hindrance, for Dreamspeakers and Ecstasy Cultists especially.<br /> <br /> All of this not even getting into Ascension War related complications that can pop up. The Technocracy monitors airports and other major transit hubs. Depending on how intense the Technocracy/Tradition/Disparate political climate is at the time, it could either make it very difficult to travel for any Traditionalist, or just for those the Union particularly hates. Even Technocrats might have trouble moving around, if there's a bit of internal Union skullduggery afoot.<br /> <br /> Given that Mages are often multicultural figures, they might have trouble crossing borders. Getting in legally can be a pain, and staying for long periods can require further headaches. Plus, you're a known quality to the local authorities, mundane or otherwise. They can even deny the Mage entry if they think the Mage is suspicious, or has a shady history. If the Shaman from earlier had an unfortunate stint in an asylum (not uncommon for those who Awakened into Spirit power), that can come up. Getting in illegally has its own set of difficulties and risks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}